## Solution Code (Python 3 version using `eval()` safely)
Even though the original HackerRank problem is *Python 2 only*, this version works in **Python 3** using `eval`.

code:

x, k = map(int, input().split())           # Read x and k
poly = input()                             # Read polynomial as string
result = eval(poly)                        # Evaluate polynomial at x , # eval() will use the current value of x from our variable
print(result == k)                         # Compare#print(result == k) Because it prints: True → if polynomial result equals k; False → otherwise
